Name: easyh5
Version: 0.9.0
Date: 2026-08-30
Title: An easy-to-use HDF5 data interface for MATLAB/Octave
Author: Qianqian Fang <fangqq@gmail.com>
Maintainer: Qianqian Fang <fangqq@gmail.com>
Description: EasyH5 is a fully automated, fast and compact HDF5 data
 interface for MATLAB and GNU Octave. It provides two functions,
 saveh5 and loadh5, to write an arbitrary MATLAB/Octave data
 structure - including nested structs, cell arrays, complex and
 sparse arrays, strings, tables and maps - to an HDF5 file, and to
 read an HDF5 file back into the equivalent data structure. Data
 types that HDF5 can not represent natively are stored using the
 JData annotation format so that they survive a round trip. In
 GNU Octave, the low-level HDF5 interface is provided by the
 oct-hdf5 package.
URL: https://github.com/NeuroJSON/easyh5
License: GPL-3.0-or-later OR BSD-3-Clause
Depends: octave (>= 5.0.0)
Categories: Data Format
